# r1114 phase 5: rerun on the R3 boot of world pwgr (after pwgr3.qb). SQ-PWG-43 B9 stayed at generated=1 for 20 reads
# in pwgr1 (pwg8 on -08: generated=2 for about 47 ticks, then 0): 60 reads tell a slow servo from a stuck one.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113pwg/pwgr3r.qb perf/runs/r1114/pwgr3r
pace 1

## SQ-PWG-43 | rerun at X 1340 Z 1700, B9 read for 60 x 5 ticks (pwgr1: generated=1 for all 20 reads): servo part only at 40 V: 0.5 V step moves about 4 RPM then idle current 0.63 A; fix B9
> forceload add 1330 1690 1355 1710
sleep 4
> zpwg3 place 1343 -60 1700 powergrid:servo facing=east
waitlog \[zpwg3\] done 20
> zpwg3 src 1340 -60 1700 40
> zpwg3 place 1340 -60 1703 powergrid:current_gauge
> zpwg3 w 1340 -60 1700 0 1340 -60 1703 0
> zpwg3 w 1340 -60 1703 1 1343 -60 1700 0
> zpwg3 w 1343 -60 1700 1 1340 -60 1700 1
> zpwg3 src 1346 -60 1703 0
> zpwg3 w 1346 -60 1703 0 1343 -60 1700 2
> zpwg3 w 1346 -60 1703 1 1343 -60 1700 1
sleep 2
> zpwg3 src 1346 -60 1703 0.5
pace 0
repeat 12
> zpwg4 kin 1343 -60 1700
sleep 0.25
end
pace 1
> zpwg3 be 1340 -60 1703
> zpwg3 be 1343 -60 1700
# fix B9: unpowered servo given a 1 V target (72 degrees), then powered again
> zpwg3 src 1340 -60 1700 0
sleep 1
> zpwg3 src 1346 -60 1703 1
sleep 2
> zpwg4 kin 1343 -60 1700
> zpwg3 src 1340 -60 1700 40
pace 0
repeat 60
> zpwg4 kin 1343 -60 1700
sleep 0.25
end
pace 1
> zpwg3 be 1340 -60 1703
> zpwg3 be 1343 -60 1700
expect \[zpwg4\] .*generated=-?[3-5](\.\d+)? overstressed
expect \[zpwg4\] .*generated=0 overstressed
reject \[zpwg\w*\] error
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look 0.5 V step: generated about +-4 within 10 ticks, 0 after about 35 ticks, then gauge about 0.63 A (idle coil); servo thermal not overheated; B9: unpowered read generated=0, powered again moves within 10 ticks for about 65 ticks, then idle current

